{% doc %}
  The Social cards grid (static block of Contact locations): one Social card per account. Only the
  Contact locations section uses it.
  - 3 cards per row from 375px (phone design); a last row that is not full is centred, so 5 cards
    give the Figma 3 + 2 (the 2 sit under the gaps). Below 375px: one card per row.
  - A wide grid (62rem, desktop): the Figma 300px cards, the first and third at the edges.
  No card: nothing on the store (the section leaves this part out), a note in the theme editor.

  @example
  {% content_for 'block', type: '_social-list', id: 'social' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- comment -%}
  Two elements on purpose: a container query styles what's INSIDE the container, never the container
  itself, so the outer div is the container and the inner one is the grid it changes.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture cards_html -%}{% content_for 'blocks' %}{%- endcapture -%}

<div class="social-list" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <div class="social-list__grid">
    {{ cards_html }}
    {%- unless cards_html contains 'class="social-card' -%}
      {%- if request.design_mode -%}
        <p class="social-list__note">{{ 'contact.locations.social_editor_empty' | t }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .social-list {
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  /*
    Flex rows with a centred last row: with equal cards and equal gaps, two cards in a row of three
    sit exactly under the two gaps above them (Figma 3 + 2), for any number of cards.
  */
  .social-list__grid {
    --social-columns: 1;
    --social-gap: var(--space-sm);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--social-gap);
  }

  .social-list__grid > * {
    flex: 0 0 calc((100% - (var(--social-columns) - 1) * var(--social-gap)) / var(--social-columns));
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 375px) {
    .social-list__grid {
      --social-columns: 3;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    .social-list__grid {
      --social-gap: var(--space-lg);
    }
  }

  /* Wide: 300 Figma px cards (Figma 262, enlarged), the gaps take the rest (first and third card at the edges) */
  @container (min-width: 62rem) {
    .social-list__grid {
      --social-card-w: max(16.375rem, calc(300 * var(--px, 0.0625rem)));
      column-gap: calc((100% - 3 * var(--social-card-w)) / 2);
      row-gap: var(--space-2xl); /* 42px */
    }

    .social-list__grid > * {
      flex-basis: var(--social-card-w);
    }
  }

  /* Reveal one after the other in each group of five */
  .social-list__grid > :nth-child(5n + 2) { --animate-delay: 100ms; }
  .social-list__grid > :nth-child(5n + 3) { --animate-delay: 200ms; }
  .social-list__grid > :nth-child(5n + 4) { --animate-delay: 300ms; }
  .social-list__grid > :nth-child(5n + 5) { --animate-delay: 400ms; }

  .social-list__note {
    flex-basis: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border);
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: center;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:general.social_list",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [{ "type": "_social-card" }],
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
